# --- Generated world ---
# Everything here is a build artefact, reproduced exactly from WorldSettings by
# "VibeRide > Build World Scene" (or the BuildAll* command-line methods). The
# terrain asset alone is ~10 MB of binary that changes on every regenerate, so
# committing it would bloat history quickly for no benefit.
#
# After cloning, run the world builder once before opening the Ride scene.
unity/Assets/Generated/
unity/Assets/Generated.meta
unity/Assets/Scenes/
unity/Assets/Scenes.meta

# --- Build output and debugging artefacts ---
unity/Captures/
*.log
# Any packaged build. The first pattern here was VibeRide-mac-*.zip, which
# did not match the versioned name the release script produces
# (VibeRide-0.1.0-mac-universal.zip) -- and a 45 MB zip went into history.
VibeRide-*.zip
VibeRide-*.pkg
VibeRide-*.dmg
KickrWorld-*.zip
report
report-*
crash-*.txt

# Downloaded asset archives. Only the models actually used are committed, under
# unity/Assets/Models/ -- see that folder's CREDITS.md. The full packs are large
# and re-downloadable from the URLs recorded there.
thirdparty/
